# The ktir-mlir-frontend commit the OpSpec->KTIR emitter is tested against.
#
# This lives here, not in pyproject.toml, on purpose.  `uv lock --check` demands
# exact correspondence between pyproject.toml and uv.lock in both directions, and
# CI runs `pre-commit run --all-files`, which ignores the `files:` gate on the
# check-requirements-dev hook.  So an unpinned URL in pyproject.toml would break
# every unrelated PR the moment this repo gets a commit, and a pinned one would
# put a top-level-approval file in the path of every routine bump.  Keeping the
# dependency out of pyproject.toml/uv.lock entirely leaves the lock check stable
# forever and makes a bump a one-line change to this file.
#
# Bump: edit the line below, then re-run tools/install-ktir.sh.
91455932139b219653f2396b0861b7aaf1961d6b
